  })
})
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure success criteria and verify no leakage over time?
- What are the trade-offs of cache effectiveness vs. isolation, and how would you monitor them?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design scalable supply chain and third-party risk controls for real-time data platforms, including attestation, signing, SBOM management, and incident response coordination with external vendors.

## Key Concepts
- Supply chain security and third-party risk management
- Artifact signing with Sigstore/cosign and SBOM generation
- Per-artifact IAM and ephemeral credentials via AWS STS
- Runtime attestation for serverless and container environments
- Incident response playbooks, containment strategies, and vendor communications

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify artifact signature and SBOM integrity before deployment
async function verifyArtifact(artifactUrl, sbomUrl, expectedDigest) {
  const artifact = await fetch(artifactUrl);
  const artifactDigest = await computeSHA256(artifact);

  if (artifactDigest !== expectedDigest) {
    throw new Error('Artifact integrity check failed');
  }

  const signature = await cosign.verify(artifact, publicKey);
  const sbom = await spdx.parse(fetch(sbomUrl));
  const components = sbom.getVulnerableDependencies();

  return { signature, components, isTrusted: signature.valid };
}
```
